{"learnerLanguage":"pt","spokenSeconds":200,"turns":[{"speaker":"character","text":"Good morning. My name is Mark. Can you tell me your full name?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Good morning, my name is Rafael Costa."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Let's talk about where you live. Do you live in a house or an apartment?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I live in an apartment in Curitiba, it's not very big but it's quite comfortable and it's close to my office, so I can walk to work, which is a big advantage."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Would you like to move somewhere else in the future?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Maybe, yes. I've been thinking about moving to a smaller city, because Curitiba is getting more expensive and the traffic is getting worse every year. But on the other hand, my job is here, so it's a difficult decision."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Describe a piece of technology you use every day. Say what it is, how often you use it, what you use it for, and explain how your life would be different without it."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Well, I'm going to talk about my smartphone, which is probably the thing I use more in my day. I use it since I wake up until I go to sleep, for example to check emails, to read the news and to talk with my family. I also use it for pay things, because in Brazil we use a lot a system called Pix. Without it, my life would be much more complicated, because I would need to carry money and I would lose contact with some friends who live far away. But sometimes I think I depend on it too much."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Do you think people spend too much time on their phones?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Definitely. I notice that when I go out with friends, everybody is looking at the phone instead of talking. I think it's affecting the way we relate with each other, especially the teenagers, who grew up with this technology."},{"speaker":"character","text":"What could schools do about this?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"In my opinion, schools could limit the use of phones in the classroom, but they should also teach students how to use technology in a responsible way, because banning it completely is not realistic nowadays."}],"criteria":[{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"fluencyCoherence","levelBand":null,"name":"Fluency and Coherence","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"lexicalResource","levelBand":null,"name":"Lexical Resource","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"grammar","levelBand":null,"name":"Grammatical Range and Accuracy","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"pronunciation","levelBand":null,"name":"Pronunciation","scope":"task","sound":true,"voiceOnly":true}],"task":{"brief":"The test's three parts in a shorter call","minutes":{"max":5,"min":5},"name":"Speaking mock","role":"examiner"},"title":"IELTS Speaking","exam":"ielts"}